					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/t-rutherford" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4620432); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4620432&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834562" alt="T Rutherford" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4620432)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/t-rutherford" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4620432); return false;" >T Rutherford</a></span> <span class="odate time_1561603767 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Jun 2019 02:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4292212">
									

<p>Good concept, but this article needs some more work.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Crit&nbsp;here</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Crit&nbsp;here</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It's clear you've put in a lot of work on this, but a lot of the grammar and syntax choices are very difficult to overlook. Use of certain words like &quot;striking&quot; and &quot;absolutely&quot; make the article feel less clinical than it should be. Dr.Calloway instead of Dr. Calloway, overuse of the word &quot;instances&quot;, etc. The article would have benefited from another 2 or 3 passes for revision.</p>
<p>&quot;Cuckoo wasps are related to over species of 3000 bees, wasps, and other insects, primarily through their physique and personality. One of the most striking physical features of the species is their shiny metallic carapaces, which have been designed with microscopic structures so thin they interfere with visible light.&quot; Explaining the non-anomalous species outside of footnotes, or in direct contrast to the scip, feels out of place, even as a run-up to it's differences.</p>
<p>The article tends to be a bit redundant. A lot of the narrative you're trying to show the reader could be condensed. Especially the test logs, and double MTF logs.</p>
<p>All that said, you're on the verge of a really good article. MTF logs are strong, but the dialogue tone tends to jump around a bit. The closing addendum is equally provocative, but the escalation and contrast feel unbelievable. Dr. Calloway comes in like a bat out of hell, but Johanson remains cool and collected the entire time.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, in it's current state, it's a no vote for me. Keep at it though, there's a lot of potential here.</p>

							</div>

								
					
